    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d960">

                <pb facs="1080" n="936" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg936"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.05/288: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-09T11:00:00-05:00">January 9, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. The Department would be glad, before formulating a reply to the note of
                    October 28, 1928, from the Egyptian Government,<anchor n="6" xml:id="d960-f1"/>
                    to receive the recommendations of the Legation mentioned in your despatch No.
                    89, December 1.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d960-f2"/> If the recommendations have been
                    set forth in a despatch, when was it mailed? If this has not been mailed
                    already, please briefly telegraph the recommendations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
